content.reasoning:
The body preview in the execute result already gives me what I need. Let me parse it:

```
{
  "resources": {
    "vehicle_positions": {
      "canonical": "/v3/positions",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v1/locations", "/v2/pings"]
    },
    "trip_history": {
      "canonical": "/v3/trips",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v1/journeys"],
      "not": "/v2/routes (planned routes)"
    },
    "sensor_frames": {
      "canonical": "/v3/sensor-frames",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v2/sensors"]
    },
    "geofence_events": {
      "canonical": "/v3/geofence-events",
      "not": "/v3/geofences (definitions)"
    }
  }
}
```

For `sensor_frames`:
- canonical: `/v3/sensor-frames`
- deprecated_aliases: `["/v2/sensors"]` — and only one alias listed

The user wants:
- canonical_path: the canonical path the binding should wire to (per-frame source)
- deprecated_alias: the deprecated rollup alias listed in the catalog

So:
- canonical_path: "/v3/sensor-frames"
- deprecated_alias: "/v2/sensors"

This matches the spec too: `/v3/sensor-frames` is "Canonical OBD sensor frames" and `/v2/sensors` is "Legacy aggregate sensor readings (deprecated)" — so /v2/sensors is the aggregate rollup alias.

